The diff does what #977 layer 3 asked.
• Sub-agents spawned by a pinned-directory parent (spawn workers) now refuse the same git redirection escapes the parent refuses (--git-dir, -C, GIT_DIR=).
• The refusal goes through the parent's own detector and message, so the policy and the wording are shared. The tests compare the child's refusal text to the parent's actual refusal with assert_eq!, for both the sub-agent and the read-only explore agent.
• When there is no pin, which is every ordinary session, the check is never called and the child's bash is built exactly as before. Tests cover that case too.

Reachability holds. src/commands_spawn.rs:877 and :1028 set the pinned directory on a worker's config, and that config's agent build adds both sub_agent and explore_agent (src/agent_builder.rs:1266 and :1317). So the case the task targets really happens.

